SUMMARY:Green River from Bishop Branch FITNESS Hike\, 10.5mi\; 2\,200ft
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nWe head to the tropical part of WN
 C where we may see more foliage and flowers in bloom. The road is now repa
 ired and the trails mostly cleared out. Our route includes waterfalls\, ca
 scades\, and rushing water. There will be a few manageable water crossings
 . See map here: https://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/custom-rou
 te-74a221c\n\nThis route differs from our usual one in the Green River are
 a\, avoiding the fairly dangerous washouts along the Pulliam Creek Trail. 
 We will not do the Narrows rope climb this time.\n\n...If you sign up and 
 change your mind even if on waitlist\, change your RSVP to "not attending"
  to free up your reservation. Any rain cancellation will be posted by 7:30
 am.\n\nPACE: All fitness hikes have a brisk steady pace (\\~3 mi/hr)\, adj
 usting for trail conditions\, and regrouping as needed. These hikes are sp
 ecifically for conditioned hikers. Please be sure of your hiking ability b
 efore signing on.\n\nCAR POOL: Those who wish to car pool can meet at West
 gate Plaza\, directly across the lot from Earth Fare\, near the EV charger
 s\, at 8:45am. Please tell the hike leader where you intend to meet the gr
 oup: Westgate (8:45) or Bishop Branch Trailhead (9:30).\n\nDIRECTIONS to T
 RAILHEAD: From Asheville\, travel south (ah hem\, "east") on I-26 past Hen
 dersonville to the Flat Rock area. Get off the interstate at Exit 53 and t
 urn left (east) onto Upward Road. Stay on Upward Road for 1.7mi. passing a
 pple orchards. Just past the Upward Holiness Baptist Church turn right ont
 o Big Hungry Road. Stay on Big Hungry Road for almost 5 miles but be alert
  and follow the signs for Big Hungry. (At times\, continuation on Big Hung
 ry looks more like a turn off the main road.) Pass our usual trailhead and
  continue to the next one. Photo is of the Bishop Branch Trailhead.\n\nDog
 s are welcome\, but have a leash handy in case we run into other hikers or
  dogs.\n\nRelease of Liability:\nThe organizer of this trip is a volunteer
  and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to or
 ganize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowle
 dge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\
 , illnesses and damages arising from\, as a result of and associated with 
 this event. In addition\, you acknowledging that you agree to the Meetup t
 erms: https://www.meetup.com/terms
